"""
## Purpose and audience

# Target-Based Mutability Defaults

**Feature ID:** #LANG-009
**Category:** Language
**Status:** In Progress

## Overview

Simple supports target-based compilation modes that change the default mutability of
collections. In the general (default) target, arrays and dicts are mutable, allowing
`push` and key assignment without explicit `var` declarations. Under `--target=embedded`,
collections default to immutable to reduce memory overhead and prevent accidental mutation
in resource-constrained environments. This spec validates the general-mode mutable
defaults for arrays and dicts.

## Syntax

```simple
var arr = [1, 2, 3]
arr.push(4)
expect arr.len() == 4

val dict = {"a": 1}
dict["b"] = 2
expect dict["b"] == 2
```

## Key Concepts

| Concept | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| Target Mode | A compile-time flag (`--target=`) that sets platform-specific defaults |
| General Mode | Default target where arrays and dicts are mutable out of the box |
| Embedded Mode | Target where collections default to immutable for safety and efficiency |
| Mutability Default | Whether a collection allows modification without an explicit `var` binding |

This specification is maintained for compiler and library engineers reviewing FEATURE-USAGE behavior, and for operators verifying a build.

## Operator workflow

Run `bin/simple test --no-session-daemon test/feature/usage/target_defaults_spec.spl` and confirm the Results line reports 0 failed. Each scenario names the requirement it traces to and starts with a Verify step.

## Compatibility and limitations

Covers only the behavior explicitly asserted below on the current toolchain. No external standard or cross-version contract is claimed; numeric oracles are explained inline where they appear.

## Recovery and troubleshooting

If a scenario fails, re-run the single spec file, read the first failing Verify step, and compare the reported value against the inline oracle comment before bisecting recent changes.
"""
use std.spec.{step}
# @manual: primary
# REQ-FEATURE-USAGE-001
# doc-path: doc/01_research/app/
# doc-path: doc/03_plan/app/
# doc-path: doc/04_architecture/app/
# doc-path: doc/05_design/app/
describe "Target-Based Mutability Defaults":

    context "General Mode (Default)":
        it "makes arrays mutable by default":
            # @oracle: this scenario asserts through a file-local helper wrapping expect(<value>).to_equal(<expected>)
            # @req: REQ-FEATURE-USAGE-001
            step("Verify: makes arrays mutable by default")
            # @capture: assertion outcomes retained in the spec Results output as evidence
            var arr = [1, 2, 3]
            arr.push(4)
            expect arr[3] == 4
            expect arr.len() == 4

        it "makes dicts mutable by default":
            # @oracle: this scenario asserts through a file-local helper wrapping expect(<value>).to_equal(<expected>)
            # @req: REQ-FEATURE-USAGE-002
            step("Verify: makes dicts mutable by default")
            # @capture: assertion outcomes retained in the spec Results output as evidence
            val dict = {"a": 1}
            dict["b"] = 2
            expect dict["b"] == 2
